  "body": "> To hide all popovers until, given an [HTML element](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#html-elements) or [Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#document) endpoint, a boolean focusPreviousElement, and a boolean fireEvents:\r\n> \r\n> 1. Let document be endpoint's [node document](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document).\r\n> 2. Let closeAllOpenPopovers be an algorithm which performs the following steps:\r\n> 2. 1. Let popover be document's [topmost auto popover](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#topmost-auto-popover).\r\n> 2. 2. While popover is not null:\r\n> 2. 2. 1. Run the [hide popover algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#hide-popover-algorithm) given popover, focusPreviousElement, fireEvents, and false.\r\n> 2. 2. 2. Set popover to document's [topmost auto popover](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#topmost-auto-popover).\r\n> 3. If endpoint is null, then run closeAllOpenPopovers and return.\r\n\r\nSo \"endpoint\" can be null, so how does steps 1. & 2. get the document? Does that algorithm need to always take a document as extra argument?\r\n\r\ncc @josepharhar @mfreed7 @domenic ",
